{"code":"fr","name":"French","native":"Français","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"A1","pronunciation":{"title":"Sound French from day one","rules":[{"rule":"Final letters are usually silent","explain":"PARIS is pah-REE (no S). PETIT is puh-TEE (no T). Read the middle, drop the tail.","examples":[{"t":"Paris","r":"pah-REE","en":"Paris"},{"t":"petit","r":"puh-TEE","en":"small"}]},{"rule":"Nasal vowels hum through the nose","explain":"ON (bon), AN (enfant), IN (vin) hum like a blocked nose. BON = boh(n) — don't pop the N!","examples":[{"t":"bon","r":"boh(n)","en":"good"},{"t":"vin","r":"va(n)","en":"wine"}]},{"rule":"R comes from the throat","explain":"Gargle a soft R at the back: ROUGE = rroozh. Never roll it Spanish-style.","examples":[{"t":"rouge","r":"rroozh","en":"red"},{"t":"rue","r":"rew","en":"street"}]},{"rule":"U vs OU are different sounds","explain":"OU = oo (LOU). U = tight lips, say EE: RUE (street) vs ROUE (wheel). Round your lips hard!","examples":[{"t":"rue","r":"rew","en":"street"},{"t":"tout","r":"too","en":"all"}]},{"rule":"Stress the last syllable","explain":"French leans forward: BONJOUR = boh(n)-ZHOOR, MERCI = mair-SEE. The end is always strongest.","examples":[{"t":"bonjour","r":"boh(n)-ZHOOR","en":"hello"},{"t":"merci","r":"mair-SEE","en":"thanks"}]}]},"alphabet":{"title":"The French alphabet: 26 letters","explain":"Same letters as English, but the NAMES sound French. Learn them to spell your name aloud: JE M'APPELLE … (my name is …), ÇA S'ÉPELLE … (it is spelled …).","letters":[{"t":"a","r":"ah","tip":"as in father: AMI"},{"t":"b","r":"beh","tip":"short and soft: BON"},{"t":"c","r":"seh","tip":"CA=K, CE/CI=S: CE"},{"t":"d","r":"deh","tip":"soft D: DEUX"},{"t":"e","r":"uh","tip":"soft grunt: PETIT"},{"t":"f","r":"eff","tip":"same as English: FILLE"},{"t":"g","r":"zheh","tip":"GA=hard G, GE=ZH: GARE"},{"t":"h","r":"ahsh","tip":"always silent: HOMME = om"},{"t":"i","r":"ee","tip":"as in machine: ICI"},{"t":"j","r":"zhee","tip":"ZH sound: JOUR"},{"t":"k","r":"kah","tip":"rare, foreign words: KILO"},{"t":"l","r":"ell","tip":"same as English: LIVRE"},{"t":"m","r":"emm","tip":"same as English: MAIN"},{"t":"n","r":"enn","tip":"same as English: NON"},{"t":"o","r":"oh","tip":"round O: MOT"},{"t":"p","r":"peh","tip":"same, less puff: PAIN"},{"t":"q","r":"kew","tip":"always QU = K: QUATRE"},{"t":"r","r":"air","tip":"throaty R: ROUGE"},{"t":"s","r":"ess","tip":"S, or Z between vowels: ROSE"},{"t":"t","r":"teh","tip":"same as English: TABLE"},{"t":"u","r":"ew","tip":"tight lips EE: RUE"},{"t":"v","r":"veh","tip":"same as English: VIN"},{"t":"w","r":"doo-bluh-veh","tip":"double V: WAGON"},{"t":"x","r":"eeks","tip":"KS: TAXI"},{"t":"y","r":"ee-grek","tip":"Greek I: YAOURT"},{"t":"z","r":"zedd","tip":"Z sound: ZÉRO"}]},"counting":{"title":"Counting 0 to 100","explain":"Learn 0–16 by heart. 17–19 = DIX + number (dix-sept). 20–69 are regular (trente-deux). Then the famous twists: 70 = 60+10, 80 = 4×20, 90 = 4×20+10!","numbers":[{"t":"zéro","r":"zeh-ROH","en":"0"},{"t":"un","r":"uhn","en":"1"},{"t":"deux","r":"duh","en":"2"},{"t":"trois","r":"trwah","en":"3"},{"t":"quatre","r":"katr","en":"4"},{"t":"cinq","r":"sa(n)k","en":"5"},{"t":"six","r":"sees","en":"6"},{"t":"sept","r":"set","en":"7"},{"t":"huit","r":"weet","en":"8"},{"t":"neuf","r":"nuff","en":"9"},{"t":"dix","r":"dees","en":"10"},{"t":"onze","r":"oh(n)z","en":"11"},{"t":"douze","r":"dooz","en":"12"},{"t":"treize","r":"trez","en":"13"},{"t":"quatorze","r":"kah-TORZ","en":"14"},{"t":"quinze","r":"ka(n)z","en":"15"},{"t":"seize","r":"sez","en":"16"},{"t":"dix-sept","r":"dee-SET","en":"17"},{"t":"dix-huit","r":"dee-ZWEET","en":"18"},{"t":"dix-neuf","r":"dee-ZNUFF","en":"19"},{"t":"vingt","r":"va(n)","en":"20"},{"t":"trente","r":"trah(n)t","en":"30"},{"t":"quarante","r":"kah-rah(n)t","en":"40"},{"t":"cinquante","r":"sa(n)-kah(n)t","en":"50"},{"t":"soixante","r":"swah-sah(n)t","en":"60"},{"t":"soixante-dix","r":"swah-sah(n)t-DEES","en":"70 (60+10)"},{"t":"quatre-vingts","r":"katr-VA(n)","en":"80 (4×20)"},{"t":"quatre-vingt-dix","r":"katr-va(n)-DEES","en":"90 (4×20+10)"},{"t":"cent","r":"sah(n)","en":"100"}],"rules":["70 = soixante-dix (60+10): soixante et onze = 71.","80 = quatre-vingts (4×20): drops S when followed: quatre-vingt-deux = 82.","90 = quatre-vingt-dix (4×20+10): quatre-vingt-quinze = 95."]},"level":{"title":"Beginner: first words, family, food","goals":["Greet people and introduce yourself in French","Count, tell age, and talk about family","Order food and use basic present-tense verbs"],"units":[{"id":"A1-U1","title":"First words","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U1-L1","title":"Bonjour! Greetings and politeness","learn":"BONJOUR works all day until evening, then BONSOIR. SALUT is hello/bye for friends. Magic trio: S'IL VOUS PLAÎT (please), MERCI (thanks), PARDON (sorry). AU REVOIR closes every meeting.","vocab":[{"t":"bonjour","r":"boh(n)-ZHOOR","en":"hello / good morning","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"bonsoir","r":"boh(n)-SWAHR","en":"good evening","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"salut","r":"sah-LEW","en":"hi / bye (friends)","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"au revoir","r":"oh ruh-VWAHR","en":"goodbye","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"s'il vous plaît","r":"seel voo PLEH","en":"please (formal)","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"merci","r":"mair-SEE","en":"thanks","pos":"noun"},{"t":"pardon","r":"pahr-DOH(n)","en":"sorry / excuse me","pos":"noun"},{"t":"excusez-moi","r":"eks-kew-zeh-MWAH","en":"excuse me","pos":"verb"}],"grammar":{"title":"Every noun is LE or LA (un/une)","explain":"Masculine nouns take LE/UN, feminine take LA/UNE. Learn every noun WITH its article: LE livre, LA maison. No shortcuts — gender is half the word!","pattern":"un/le + masculine · une/la + feminine","examples":[{"t":"le livre","r":"luh LEEVR","en":"the book"},{"t":"la maison","r":"lah meh-ZOH(n)","en":"the house"},{"t":"un café","r":"uhn kah-FEH","en":"a coffee"}],"mistakes":["Saying LA livre — livre is masculine: LE livre.","Skipping articles (saying just Maison) — always LE/LA/UN/UNE."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Léa","t":"Bonjour! Comment ça va?","r":"boh(n)-ZHOOR! koh-mah(n) sah VAH?","en":"Hello! How are you?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Très bien, merci. Et vous?","r":"treh bya(n), mair-SEE. eh voo?","en":"Very well, thanks. And you?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Bien, merci. Au revoir!","r":"bya(n), mair-SEE. oh ruh-VWAHR!","en":"Fine, thanks. Goodbye!"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Au revoir!","r":"oh ruh-VWAHR!","en":"Goodbye!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: hello","answer":"bonjour"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: thank you","answer":"merci"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ revoir (goodbye)","answer":"au"},{"type":"choose","q":"Which means 'please' (formal)?","options":["merci","s'il vous plaît","bonjour","pardon"],"answer":"s'il vous plaît"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Bonjour, merci.","answer":"Bonjour, merci."}],"quiz":[{"q":"BONJOUR is used…","options":["only mornings","all day until evening","only nights","never"],"answer":1,"why":"Bonjour = hello until evening."},{"q":"SALUT is for…","options":["bosses","friends","strangers","kings"],"answer":1,"why":"Salut = casual hi/bye."},{"q":"LE LIVRE means…","options":["the house","the book","the coffee","the door"],"answer":1,"why":"Livre (masculine) = book."},{"q":"Which is feminine?","options":["le livre","la maison","le café","le pain"],"answer":1,"why":"La marks feminine nouns."},{"q":"PARDON means…","options":["please","thanks","sorry","hello"],"answer":2,"why":"Pardon = sorry/excuse me."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Greetings worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Match the greeting to its use.","items":["bonjour","bonsoir","salut"],"key":["hello (daytime)","good evening","hi/bye (friends)"]},{"instruction":"Fill in: le or la.","items":["___ maison","___ livre","___ table"],"key":["la","le","la"]},{"instruction":"Write the magic words.","items":["please","thanks","sorry"],"key":["s'il vous plaît","merci","pardon"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U1-L2","title":"Numbers and introductions","learn":"Numbers 1–10 open prices and ages. Introduce with ÊTRE (to be): JE SUIS = I am. Je suis Léa. Ask names: COMMENT TU T'APPELLES? (What are you called?). Answer: JE M'APPELLE …","vocab":[{"t":"un","r":"uhn","en":"one","pos":"number"},{"t":"deux","r":"duh","en":"two","pos":"number"},{"t":"trois","r":"trwah","en":"three","pos":"number"},{"t":"quatre","r":"katr","en":"four","pos":"number"},{"t":"cinq","r":"sa(n)k","en":"five","pos":"number"},{"t":"six","r":"sees","en":"six","pos":"number"},{"t":"sept","r":"set","en":"seven","pos":"number"},{"t":"huit","r":"weet","en":"eight","pos":"number"},{"t":"neuf","r":"nuff","en":"nine","pos":"number"},{"t":"dix","r":"dees","en":"ten","pos":"number"}],"grammar":{"title":"ÊTRE: je suis, tu es, il/elle est","explain":"JE SUIS = I am, TU ES = you are, IL/ELLE EST = he/she is. French always keeps the pronoun (JE, TU, IL) — never drop it like Spanish!","pattern":"je suis · tu es · il/elle est","examples":[{"t":"Je suis Léa.","r":"zhuh swee leh-AH.","en":"I am Léa."},{"t":"Tu es Théo?","r":"tew eh teh-OH?","en":"Are you Théo?"},{"t":"Elle est française.","r":"ell eh frah(n)-SEZ.","en":"She is French."}],"mistakes":["Dropping JE (saying SUIS Léa) — French needs JE SUIS.","Saying IL for a woman — she is ELLE."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Léa","t":"Salut, je suis Léa. Comment tu t'appelles?","r":"sah-LEW, zhuh swee leh-AH. koh-mah(n) tew tah-PELL?","en":"Hi, I am Léa. What is your name?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Je m'appelle Théo. Tu es d'où?","r":"zhuh mah-PELL teh-OH. tew eh DOO?","en":"My name is Théo. Where are you from?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Je suis de Paris.","r":"zhuh swee duh pah-REE.","en":"I am from Paris."},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Enchanté!","r":"ah(n)-shah(n)-TEH!","en":"Nice to meet you!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am Léa","answer":"Je suis Léa"},{"type":"fill","q":"Tu ___ Théo? (are)","answer":"es"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I am' in French is…","options":["est","es","suis (with je)","sont"],"answer":"suis (with je)"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: suis / je / Léa","answer":"je suis Léa"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Je m'appelle Théo.","answer":"Je m'appelle Théo."}],"quiz":[{"q":"JE SUIS means…","options":["you are","I am","he is","we are"],"answer":1,"why":"Je suis = I am."},{"q":"How do you ask someone's name (casual)?","options":["Comment ça va?","Comment tu t'appelles?","Tu es d'où?","Quel âge?"],"answer":1,"why":"Comment tu t'appelles? = What are you called?"},{"q":"CINQ is number…","options":["3","4","5","6"],"answer":2,"why":"un deux trois quatre CINQ."},{"q":"'I am from Paris' is…","options":["Je suis Paris","Je suis de Paris","Je de Paris suis","Est de Paris"],"answer":1,"why":"Je suis DE + place."},{"q":"ENCHANTÉ means…","options":["goodbye","nice to meet you","good luck","see you"],"answer":1,"why":"Say it when you first meet."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Numbers and names worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Write the numbers in French.","items":["2","5","10"],"key":["deux","cinq","dix"]},{"instruction":"Complete with suis, es, or est.","items":["Je ___ Léa (I am)","Tu ___ Théo? (are you)","Elle ___ française (she is)"],"key":["suis","es","est"]},{"instruction":"Introduce yourself in two lines.","items":["Say your name","Say where you are from"],"key":["Je suis …","Je suis de …"]}]}}]},{"id":"A1-U2","title":"Daily life","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U2-L1","title":"Family and AVOIR (age)","learn":"Meet the family: MÈRE, PÈRE, FRÈRE, SŒUR. Age uses AVOIR (to have): J'AI DIX ANS = I have 10 years = I am 10. Ask: TU AS QUEL ÂGE? (You have what age?)","vocab":[{"t":"la mère","r":"lah mair","en":"mother","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le père","r":"luh pair","en":"father","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le frère","r":"luh frair","en":"brother","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la sœur","r":"lah surr","en":"sister","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le fils","r":"luh fees","en":"son","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la fille","r":"lah fee","en":"daughter","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la famille","r":"lah fah-MEE","en":"family","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'ami / l'amie","r":"lah-MEE","en":"friend (m/f)","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"AVOIR for age: j'ai… ans","explain":"J'AI = I have, TU AS = you have, IL/ELLE A = he/she has. Age: J'AI + number + ANS. TU AS QUEL ÂGE? = How old are you?","pattern":"j'ai/tu as/il a + number + ans","examples":[{"t":"J'ai dix ans.","r":"zheh dees ah(n).","en":"I am 10 years old."},{"t":"Tu as quel âge?","r":"tew ah kel AHZH?","en":"How old are you?"},{"t":"Ma sœur a sept ans.","r":"mah surr ah set ah(n).","en":"My sister is 7."}],"mistakes":["Saying JE SUIS dix ans — age always uses AVOIR.","Saying AN without S: ANS sounds ahn — keep the S silent!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Léa","t":"Tu as des frères?","r":"tew ah deh frair?","en":"Do you have brothers/sisters?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Oui, j'ai un frère et une sœur.","r":"wee, zheh uhn frair eh ewn surr.","en":"Yes, I have one brother and one sister."},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Ta sœur a quel âge?","r":"tah surr ah kel AHZH?","en":"How old is your sister?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Elle a sept ans.","r":"ell ah set ah(n).","en":"She is seven."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am 10 years old","answer":"J'ai dix ans"},{"type":"fill","q":"Ma sœur ___ sept ans. (has)","answer":"a"},{"type":"choose","q":"'How old are you?' is…","options":["Comment ça va?","Tu as quel âge?","Comment tu t'appelles?","Tu es d'où?"],"answer":"Tu as quel âge?"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: ans / ai / dix / j'","answer":"j'ai dix ans"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: J'ai un frère.","answer":"J'ai un frère."}],"quiz":[{"q":"J'AI DIX ANS means…","options":["I have ten houses","I am ten years old","I like ten songs","I see ten birds"],"answer":1,"why":"Avoir + ans = age."},{"q":"LA SŒUR is…","options":["brother","sister","mother","daughter"],"answer":1,"why":"Sœur = sister."},{"q":"Which asks about age?","options":["Comment ça va?","Tu as quel âge?","Tu habites où?","Quelle heure?"],"answer":1,"why":"Quel âge = what age."},{"q":"'My sister is 7' is…","options":["Ma sœur a sept ans","Ma sœur est sept","Ma sœur sept ans","J'ai sœur sept"],"answer":0,"why":"A + number + ans."},{"q":"UN FRÈRE ET UNE SŒUR means…","options":["two brothers","two sisters","a brother and a sister","no siblings"],"answer":2,"why":"Un = a (m), une = a (f)."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Family worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["mother","brother","family"],"key":["la mère","le frère","la famille"]},{"instruction":"Write the age sentence.","items":["I am 8 (years)","My brother is 5"],"key":["J'ai huit ans","Mon frère a cinq ans"]},{"instruction":"Answer about yourself.","items":["Tu as des frères?","Tu as quel âge?"],"key":["Oui/Non, (j'ai…)","J'ai … ans"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U2-L2","title":"Food and -ER verbs","learn":"Food first! EAU, PAIN, LAIT, POMME. Order with JE VOUDRAIS (I would like): JE VOUDRAIS UN CAFÉ. Most verbs end in -ER: PARLER → JE PARLE, TU PARLES, IL PARLE (all sound the same: parl!).","vocab":[{"t":"l'eau","r":"loh","en":"water","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le pain","r":"luh pa(n)","en":"bread","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le lait","r":"luh leh","en":"milk","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la pomme","r":"lah pohm","en":"apple","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le riz","r":"luh ree","en":"rice","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le poulet","r":"luh poo-LEH","en":"chicken","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le café","r":"luh kah-FEH","en":"coffee","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le thé","r":"luh teh","en":"tea","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Present -ER: je parle, tu parles, il parle","explain":"Drop -ER, add -E, -ES, -E. All three sound the same (parl)! Spelling differs, sound doesn't. PARLER, MANGER, AIMER — hundreds of verbs, one music.","pattern":"stem + e/es/e (all sound the same)","examples":[{"t":"Je parle français.","r":"zhuh parl frah(n)-SEH.","en":"I speak French."},{"t":"Tu parles anglais?","r":"tew parl ah(n)-GLEH?","en":"Do you speak English?"},{"t":"Elle chante bien.","r":"ell shah(n)t bya(n).","en":"She sings well."}],"mistakes":["Pronouncing the -S in TU PARLES — silent! All sound parl.","Saying PARLE without JE — French keeps its pronouns."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Théo","t":"Bonjour! Je voudrais un café, s'il vous plaît.","r":"boh(n)-ZHOOR! zhuh voo-DREH uhn kah-FEH, seel voo PLEH.","en":"Hello! I would like a coffee, please."},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Grand ou petit?","r":"grah(n) oo puh-TEE?","en":"Large or small?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Grand, merci. C'est combien?","r":"grah(n), mair-SEE. seh koh(n)-BYA(n)?","en":"Large, thanks. How much is it?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Deux euros.","r":"duh uh-ROH.","en":"Two euros."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I speak French","answer":"Je parle français"},{"type":"fill","q":"Tu ___ anglais? (speak)","answer":"parles"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I would like a coffee' starts with…","options":["Je veux","Je voudrais","J'ai","Je suis"],"answer":"Je voudrais"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: café / voudrais / un / je","answer":"je voudrais un café"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Je voudrais un thé, s'il vous plaît.","answer":"Je voudrais un thé, s'il vous plaît."}],"quiz":[{"q":"TU PARLES sounds like…","options":["par-less","parl (S silent)","par-leez","par-less-uh"],"answer":1,"why":"Final S is silent."},{"q":"LE POULET is…","options":["bread","rice","chicken","apple"],"answer":2,"why":"Poulet = chicken."},{"q":"C'EST COMBIEN? means…","options":["Where is it?","How much is it?","What time is it?","Who is it?"],"answer":1,"why":"Combien = how much."},{"q":"'She sings well' is…","options":["Elle chante bien","Elle chantes bien","Elle chanter bien","Elle chant bien"],"answer":0,"why":"Elle + -E: chante."},{"q":"The polite order word is…","options":["je veux","je voudrais","j'ai","donne"],"answer":1,"why":"Je voudrais = I would like."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Food worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["water","milk","apple"],"key":["l'eau","le lait","la pomme"]},{"instruction":"Conjugate PARLER.","items":["I speak","you speak","she speaks"],"key":["je parle","tu parles","elle parle"]},{"instruction":"Order politely in a café.","items":["a coffee, please","How much is it?"],"key":["Je voudrais un café, s'il vous plaît","C'est combien?"]}]}}]},{"id":"A1-U3","title":"Describing words","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U3-L1","title":"Colors and adjectives","learn":"Adjectives match gender AND usually come AFTER the noun: LA MAISON BLANCHE (the white house). Most add -E for feminine: ROUGE stays, but BLANC → BLANCHE, NOIR → NOIRE.","vocab":[{"t":"rouge","r":"rroozh","en":"red","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"bleu","r":"bluh","en":"blue","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"vert","r":"vair","en":"green","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"jaune","r":"zhohn","en":"yellow","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"blanc","r":"blah(n)","en":"white","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"noir","r":"nwahr","en":"black","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"grand","r":"grah(n)","en":"big / tall","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"petit","r":"puh-TEE","en":"small","pos":"adjective"}],"grammar":{"title":"Adjective agreement: add -E for feminine","explain":"LE livre ROUGE, LA maison ROUGE (rouge never changes!). But: BLANC → BLANCHE, NOIR → NOIRE, PETIT → PETITE. Plural adds silent -S: LES livres ROUGES.","pattern":"masculine · feminine (+E) · plural (+S, silent)","examples":[{"t":"Le livre rouge.","r":"luh LEEVR rroozh.","en":"The red book."},{"t":"La maison blanche.","r":"lah meh-ZOH(n) blah(n)sh.","en":"The white house."},{"t":"Les chaussures noires.","r":"leh shoh-SEWR nwahr.","en":"The black shoes."}],"mistakes":["Saying LA maison BLANC — feminine needs BLANCHE.","Putting colors before the noun (English order) — after!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Léa","t":"J'aime la maison blanche.","r":"zhemm lah meh-ZOH(n) blah(n)sh.","en":"I like the white house."},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Et la voiture rouge?","r":"eh lah vwah-TEWR rroozh?","en":"And the red car?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Elle est très jolie.","r":"ell eh treh zhoh-LEE.","en":"It is very pretty."},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Oui, elle est grande et rouge.","r":"wee, ell eh grah(n)d eh rroozh.","en":"Yes, it is big and red."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: the red book","answer":"le livre rouge"},{"type":"fill","q":"La maison ___ (white, feminine)","answer":"blanche"},{"type":"choose","q":"'The black shoes' is…","options":["Les chaussures noir","Les chaussures noires","La chaussure noirs","Le chaussures noire"],"answer":"Les chaussures noires"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: blanche / maison / la","answer":"la maison blanche"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: J'aime la maison blanche.","answer":"J'aime la maison blanche."}],"quiz":[{"q":"LA MAISON BLANCHE means…","options":["the white house","the black house","the big house","the red house"],"answer":0,"why":"Maison (f) + blanche."},{"q":"BLANC → BLANCHE because…","options":["it sounds nice","feminine adds -E (and sounds the C)","plural","formal"],"answer":1,"why":"Feminine ending changes sound."},{"q":"LES CHAUSSURES NOIRES: why NOIRES?","options":["it is long","feminine plural","shoes are black","all adjectives"],"answer":1,"why":"Feminine plural: -ES."},{"q":"ROUGE never changes because…","options":["it ends in E already","it is special","it is masculine","colors don't change"],"answer":0,"why":"-E adjectives: same m/f."},{"q":"Colors usually go…","options":["before the noun","after the noun","at sentence start","nowhere"],"answer":1,"why":"La maison blanche — after!"}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Colors worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["red","blue","small"],"key":["rouge","bleu","petit"]},{"instruction":"Match the adjective.","items":["le livre ___ (red)","la maison ___ (white)","les chaussures ___ (black)"],"key":["rouge","blanche","noires"]},{"instruction":"Describe two things.","items":["The white house","The red car"],"key":["la maison blanche","la voiture rouge"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U3-L2","title":"Days, months, and telling time","learn":"Days are lowercase and masculine: LE LUNDI. Time: QUELLE HEURE EST-IL? Answer: IL EST TROIS HEURES. Half: ET DEMIE — IL EST TROIS HEURES ET DEMIE.","vocab":[{"t":"lundi","r":"luhn-DEE","en":"Monday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"mardi","r":"mahr-DEE","en":"Tuesday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"mercredi","r":"mair-kruh-DEE","en":"Wednesday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"aujourd'hui","r":"oh-zhoor-DWEE","en":"today","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"demain","r":"duh-ma(n)","en":"tomorrow","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"hier","r":"yehr","en":"yesterday","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"la semaine","r":"lah suh-MEN","en":"week","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'heure","r":"lurr","en":"hour / time","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Telling time: il est… heures","explain":"IL EST UNE HEURE (1:00), IL EST DEUX HEURES (2:00). Half: ET DEMIE. Quarter: ET QUART. Always HEURE(S) — never drop it!","pattern":"il est + number + heure(s) (+ et demie)","examples":[{"t":"Il est une heure.","r":"eel eh ewn urr.","en":"It is one o'clock."},{"t":"Il est trois heures.","r":"eel eh trwah zurr.","en":"It is three o'clock."},{"t":"Il est trois heures et demie.","r":"eel eh trwah zurr eh duh-MEE.","en":"It is half past three."}],"mistakes":["Saying IL EST TROIS (no HEURES) — always add HEURES.","Capitalising days (Lundi) — French days are lowercase."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Théo","t":"Quelle heure est-il?","r":"kell urr eh-TEEL?","en":"What time is it?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Il est trois heures et demie.","r":"eel eh trwah zurr eh duh-MEE.","en":"It is half past three."},{"sp":"Théo","t":"On se voit demain?","r":"oh(n) suh vwah duh-ma(n)?","en":"Shall we meet tomorrow?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Oui, mardi à dix heures.","r":"wee, mahr-DEE ah dees urr.","en":"Yes, Tuesday at ten."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It is three o'clock","answer":"Il est trois heures"},{"type":"fill","q":"Il est une ___ (hour)","answer":"heure"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Half past three' is…","options":["Il est trois heures","Il est trois heures et demie","Il est la trois","Il est demie trois"],"answer":"Il est trois heures et demie"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: est-il / heure / quelle","answer":"quelle heure est-il"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Il est trois heures et demie.","answer":"Il est trois heures et demie."}],"quiz":[{"q":"IL EST UNE HEURE uses UNE because…","options":["one is lucky","heure is feminine","morning","all times"],"answer":1,"why":"Une heure — feminine."},{"q":"QUELLE HEURE EST-IL? means…","options":["What day is it?","What time is it?","Where are you?","How are you?"],"answer":1,"why":"Heure = hour/time."},{"q":"ET DEMIE means…","options":["and a quarter","and a half","and ten","o'clock sharp"],"answer":1,"why":"Demie = half."},{"q":"French days are written…","options":["CAPITALISED","lowercase","in English","never"],"answer":1,"why":"lundi, mardi — lowercase."},{"q":"DEMAIN means…","options":["today","tomorrow","yesterday","morning"],"answer":1,"why":"Demain = tomorrow."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Time worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["Monday","today","week"],"key":["lundi","aujourd'hui","la semaine"]},{"instruction":"Write the time.","items":["1:00","3:00","3:30"],"key":["Il est une heure","Il est trois heures","Il est trois heures et demie"]},{"instruction":"Make a plan.","items":["Shall we meet tomorrow?","Yes, Tuesday at ten"],"key":["On se voit demain?","Oui, mardi à dix heures"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"A1 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: hello","answer":"bonjour"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am Léa","answer":"Je suis Léa"},{"type":"fill","q":"J'ai ___ ans (I am 9)","answer":"neuf"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Do you speak English?'","options":["Tu parles anglais?","Je parle anglais?","Elle parle anglais?","Parler anglais?"],"answer":"Tu parles anglais?"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"C'est combien?","answer":"How much is it?"},{"type":"fill","q":"La maison ___ (white)","answer":"blanche"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: ans / ai / dix / j'","answer":"j'ai dix ans"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Je voudrais un café, s'il vous plaît.","answer":"Je voudrais un café, s'il vous plaît."},{"type":"fill","q":"Il est trois heures et ___ (half)","answer":"demie"},{"type":"choose","q":"'My sister is 7'","options":["Ma sœur a sept ans","Ma sœur est sept","Ma sœur sept ans","J'ai sœur sept"],"answer":"Ma sœur a sept ans"}]}}}